---
/**
 * A section boundary: the full-bleed hatched band, with rails and corner
 * nodes, that the drafting frame in `global.css` draws between one section
 * and the next.
 *
 * A component rather than a rule on `.section + .section` because the page
 * knows where its boundaries are and the stylesheet does not — a hero, a
 * filter bar and a results grid are three sections or two depending on what
 * the page means, and only the page can say. It carries no content and no
 * meaning, so it is hidden from assistive technology outright.
 */
---
<div class="section-sep" aria-hidden="true"><div class="section-sep-inner"></div></div>
